\title{topologyR: topologies of graphs and bitopologies of time series}
\description{
The package turns a graph into the topology generated by the closed
neighbourhoods of its vertices and computes its connected components
exactly, without enumerating the topology. For time series it builds the
horizontal and natural visibility graphs, at equally or unequally spaced
instants and with a natural criterion decided exactly under IEEE 754 double
arithmetic, and from their directed
versions the forward and backward topologies, a bitopological space, with
the Alexandrov topology of reachability and the invariants of the pair.
}
\section{Main functions}{

\code{\link[=horizontal_visibility_graph]{horizontal_visibility_graph()}} and \code{\link[=natural_visibility_graph]{natural_visibility_graph()}} build the
graphs; \code{\link[=generate_topology]{generate_topology()}} builds a topology of closed neighbourhoods
from any adjacency lists; \code{\link[=generate_alexandrov_topology]{generate_alexandrov_topology()}} builds the
Alexandrov topology of any digraph; \code{\link[=generate_bitopology]{generate_bitopology()}} runs the whole
pipeline for a series and states the time-reversal theorem;
\code{\link[=bitopology_invariants]{bitopology_invariants()}} reports the invariants of a forward-backward
pair; \code{\link[=time_reverse]{time_reverse()}} reverses a series together with its instants. The
proofs of the results the package relies on are written in the help pages
that state them, those of the exact natural criterion in
\link{natural_visibility_exactness}. The user manual is in
\code{system.file("manuals", "user_manual.pdf", package = "topologyR")}.
}

